==English==

===Etymology===
From {{uder|en|frm|elapser}}, from {{uder|en|la|elapsus}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|en|æps|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive|of time}} To [[pass]] or [[move]] [[by]].
#: {{ux|en|He allowed a month to '''elapse''' before beginning the work.}}
#: {{ux|en|Several days '''elapsed''' before they met again.}}
#* {{RQ:Landon Ethel Churchill|page=322|volume=II|passage=The week that was yet to '''elapse''', she spent in wandering through her uncle's favourite walks in hours of tearful vigil, beside his tomb, and in collecting together every trifle on which he had set a value.}}

====Synonyms====
* See [[Thesaurus:elapse]]

